#!/usr/bin/env bash
# ── The full batch: everything that tests this working tree on this Mac ────────
#
#   npm run verify              about 7 min (more after `npm run clean:e2e:ios`)
#
# Ends with the iOS simulator E2E, on a Release build of this tree made here
# first; it installs the app on the simulator. The physical Android phone suite
# tests an EAS build, not this tree, so it is printed as a follow-up.

source "$(dirname "$0")/lib/batch.sh"

unit "Types" test:types
unit "Lint" test:lint
unit "Unit + integration" test:unit
unit "Expo doctor" test:doctor
unit "Web end-to-end" test:e2e:web
unit "Performance regressions" test:perf
unit "iOS simulator end-to-end" test:e2e:ios

passed "everything that tests this working tree is green"
cat <<'NEXT'

Not covered above — these test an EAS build, so rebuild after app changes:

  npm run eas-build:perf:android   then, with the phone connected over USB:
  npm run install:perf:android     latest `perf` build onto the phone
  npm run test:perf:device         frame, start-up and memory measurements

NEXT
